---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CliSidebar from '../../../components/CliSidebar.astro';
---

<Layout title="Configuration - MEDE-CLI">
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <CliSidebar />
    <article class="docs-content prose">
      <h1>Configuring the Project</h1>
      
      <p>
        The behavior of MEDE-CLI in your local repository is governed by the <code>mede.config.json</code> file, which must reside in the root directory of your project.
      </p>

      <h2>Automatic Initialization</h2>
      <p>To generate a default configuration file automatically, run:</p>
      <pre><code>mede config init</code></pre>
      
      <p>This will create the <code>mede.config.json</code> file with basic configurations and suggest default folders and file names for your live documentation.</p>

      <h2>`mede.config.json` Structure</h2>
      <p>Here is a complete example with explanations of the fields:</p>

      <pre><code class="language-json" is:raw>{
  "language": "en",
  "docsRoot": "docs",
  "directories": {
    "meetingMinutes": "meeting-minutes",
    "architecturalDecisions": "architectural-decisions",
    "systemMaintenanceSpecifications": "maintenance-specifications",
    "deliveryLog": "delivery-log"
  },
  "fileNames": {
    "initialUnderstanding": "initial-understanding.md",
    "readme": "readme.md",
    "currentState": "current-state.md",
    "scopeAndVision": "scope-and-vision.md",
    "functionalRequirements": "functional-requirements.md",
    "nonFunctionalRequirements": "non-functional-requirements.md",
    "dataModel": "data-model.md",
    "timeline": "timeline.md"
  },
  "prefixes": {
    "meetingMinutes": "min",
    "architecturalDecisions": "adr",
    "systemMaintenanceSpecifications": "esm",
    "deliveryLog": "leg"
  },
  "llm": {
    "provider": "openai",
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "endpoint": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
    "apiKeyEnv": "OPENAI_API_KEY",
    "temperature": 0.2,
    "maxTokens": 4096,
    "timeoutMs": 60000
  }
}</code></pre>

      <h2>Core Fields</h2>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong><code>language</code>:</strong> Defines the language in which documentation is generated (e.g., <code>en</code> or <code>pt-BR</code>).</li>
        <li><strong><code>docsRoot</code>:</strong> Root directory of your documentation (usually <code>docs</code> or <code>.</code> if you keep it in the root).</li>
        <li><strong><code>directories</code>:</strong> Maps the physical directories where immutable historical logs are stored (minutes, ADRs, ESMs, delivery logs).</li>
        <li><strong><code>fileNames</code>:</strong> Defines the exact filenames of the live documents that represent your project's architectural truth.</li>
        <li><strong><code>llm</code>:</strong> Configures the artificial intelligence profile, including provider, model name, timeout values, and API key environment variable (read more in LLM Integration).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Applying Configuration Changes</h2>
      <p>If you manually change any filename or directory in <code>mede.config.json</code>, run the following command to physically sync the filesystem:</p>
      <pre><code>mede config apply</code></pre>
      <p>This command will detect the differences and safely rename the folders and files in your repository.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
